WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:06.500
The first trailer for Glass just dropped reuniting
Unbreakable's Bruce Willis and Samuel L Jackson

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.580
and adding Split's James McAvoy to the comic-book
mix.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:13.530
Yippee-ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm breaking down the Glass trailer

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.869
for intriguing details and connections you
might have missed.

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:24.320
Notice the purple glow that flashes over the
Universal logo towards the start of the trailer.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.110
That's a nice nod to the colour that's been
associated with our titular character, Glass,

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:31.960
since he first appeared in the movie Unbreakable
back in 2000.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.980
And when we see Elijah aka Mr Glass, Kevin
Wendell Crumb, and David Dunn together in

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.630
this scene, each of them is wearing their
signature colour from either Unbreakable or

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:42.630
Split.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:47.350
Glass is in purple, Dunn is in green (albeit
a very pale one), and Kevin is in yellow.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.560
These colours are also reflected in the design
of the villain and superhero in the first

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.500
comic book that a young Elijah was given by
his mother in Unbreakable.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.470
And this colour scheme is also evident in
the comic book store later in the trailer,

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.280
where the 'Heroes' section is bathed in green
light, and where the 'Villains' section is

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.420
in purple.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.080
As we know from Split, Kevin has 23 separate
personalities which were shown on Kevin's

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.720
computer plus a 24th superhuman alter ego
known as The Beast.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:18.580
And Sarah Paulson's psychiatrist character
Dr Ellie Staple already understands this.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.120
"I have no question, there are two dozen identities."

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.820
"I'm Mary Reynolds."

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.820
"Por favor, señora."

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.960
"We almost got you bro!"

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.920
"That live in that body with you."

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.390
From the trailer, it looks like we'll get
to see at least three more of Kevin's identities.There's

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.420
Mary Reynolds, a Spanish-speaking personality,
and maybe a prankster-type American guy?

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.460
Notice also the multiple toothbrushes provided
for Kevin.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.920
One for each of his personalities which is
a subtle call-back to the 23 toothbrushes

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.729
Kevin also had in Split.

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:52.220
"But what I am questioning is your belief
that you are something more than human."

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:57.229
Now, that's an interesting parallel between
Dr Staple and Kevin's former psychiatrist

00:01:57.229 --> 00:02:02.420
Dr Fletcher who also had her doubts about
whether the Beast was real or not.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.580
"I don't understand."

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.259
"He can't be real."

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:09.149
"There must be limits to what a human being
can become."

00:02:09.149 --> 00:02:14.319
Of course, we know that the Beast was very
real in Split and it seems like Mr Glass probably

00:02:14.319 --> 00:02:18.450
knows that too or perhaps he even had something
to do with Kevin's backstory.

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:23.069
There's an interesting shot of Glass looking
at a comic book where a character is prising

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:28.049
open steel bars in a shot that's very reminiscent
of the end of Split where the Beast tried

00:02:28.049 --> 00:02:31.549
to break into the cage that Casey had locked
herself into.

00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:36.209
The two wounds on Kevin's torso is another
nice detail calling back to that encounter

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:39.680
when Casey tried to shoot the Beast at point-blank
range.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.750
And Mr Glass actually refers to that moment
from Split with the line/this line/the following

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.299
line:
"And yet some of us still don't die with bullets."

00:02:48.299 --> 00:02:50.959
Glass is clearly fascinated with the Beast
and wants to meet him

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:52.540
"May I meet the Beast?"

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.989
"I hope for your sake that he likes you."

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:59.919
"That sounds like the bad guys teaming up."

00:02:59.919 --> 00:03:04.329
I wonder if by "bad guys", Glass is not just
referring to himself and the Beast joining

00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:08.980
forces, but he's actually also referring to
The Horde which is the name the news report

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.529
gave to Kevin at the end of Split.

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:14.090
"Because of his many personalities, he is
being called...

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.290
The Horde."

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:20.689
Remember also in Unbreakable, Glass is interested
in a comic book called Sentryman and the Coalition

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:21.689
of Evil.

00:03:21.689 --> 00:03:25.699
And interestingly, some of that cover appears
in the Comic-Con poster art for Glass.

00:03:25.699 --> 00:03:30.709
I have a feeling that Mr Glass is planning
to manipulate Kevin for his own ends.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:35.889
Think back to what his mother said in Unbreakable:
"There's the soldier villain who fights the

00:03:35.889 --> 00:03:42.329
hero with his hands... and then there's the
real threat-- the brilliant and evil archenemy...

00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:44.389
who fights the hero with his mind."

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:49.180
I think Glass sees himself as the brilliant
genius and Kevin as a useful powerful villain

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.150
to serve his needs.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.489
"No way!"

00:03:53.489 --> 00:03:57.549
Also key to the story is going to be Casey
who seems to be able to connect with Kevin,

00:03:57.549 --> 00:03:59.719
it appears via Hedwig in this scene.

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:03.659
Similar to how she did in Split getting him
to take her to the window in his room and

00:04:03.659 --> 00:04:05.769
give her his walkie-talkie.

00:04:05.769 --> 00:04:10.659
And returning from Unbreakable are David Dunn's
son and Elijah Prince's mother who could both

00:04:10.659 --> 00:04:15.790
hold clues or be keys to understanding how
Dunn and Glass acquired their powers and weaknesses.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:20.790
It looks like the movie will also revisit
Dunn's kryptonite, water, with him getting

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.600
attacked by the Beast possibly knocking him
into a small water tower behind him here?

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.880
The shot of the Beast knocking Dunn out of
a building window also reminds me of Unbreakable

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.170
when Dunn was pushed over a balcony into a
swimming pool.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:37.850
Also notice that Dr Staple looks to be rescuing
Dunn by pulling him out of water in this other

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:38.850
shot.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:42.230
"What do we call you, sir?"

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:46.000
"First name, Mr; last name, Glass."

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.130
This is a rather epic way to end the trailer.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:52.280
And I don't know about you, but those final
lines gave me vibes of Sidney Poitier in the

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:55.330
1960s Oscar-winning film In The Heat Of The
Night.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.720
"What did they call you up there?"

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.880
"They call me, Mr Tibbs."

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.780
So, what do you think about the Glass trailer?

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:07.400
And did you spot any other interesting details
or do you have any theories about the movie?

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:12.310
Leave your comments and thoughts below and,
if you enjoyed this, a like is really appreciated.

